  "intro": {
    "language": "en",
    "text": "David Zaslav (; born January 15, 1960) is an American media executive who was the CEO of Discovery, Inc. from 2006 to 2022, and its successor Warner Bros. Discovery from 2022 to 2026. Zaslav worked at NBCUniversal from 1989 to 2006, where he helped develop and launch the cable channels CNBC and MSNBC. He joined Discovery following his departure from NBCUniversal, where he oversaw its initial public offering in 2008 and merger with WarnerMedia on April 8, 2022. Following the merger, he remained CEO of Warner Bros. Discovery from its founding up until its sale to Paramount Skydance on October 6, 2026, after which he departed from the company.",
    "sourceId": "wikipedia-en",
    "usage": "Research excerpt; paraphrase and cross-check before publication."
  },
